  1053                              <1> ; waitk. At a console: a wait on the input handle for the time (EAX: 0
  1054                              <1> ; just looks, -1 is INFINITE), then ReadConsoleInputA for one event. The
  1055                              <1> ; wait is WaitForMultipleObjects, on v_hin alone or on v_hin and v_htm,
  1056                              <1> ; which follow each other. A timed wait (1 ms or more) sets the
  1057                              <1> ; high-resolution timer once for the whole time and waits for the input or
  1058                              <1> ; the timer, with no time of its own; without the timer it is a plain wait
  1059                              <1> ; on the input for the time, which starts again with its whole time after
  1060                              <1> ; each event passed over. Only key-down events count: their character,
  1061                              <1> ; or for the left and right arrow keys (virtual keys 25h and 27h, which
  1062                              <1> ; have none) ^B and ^F. Anything else is passed over.
  1063                              <1> ; Input that is not a console (a pipe or a file) is read a byte at a time
